      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Lichtenstein, Roy</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_org">Whitney Museum of American Art</category>
      <category domain="">Pop Art</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Da Corte, Alex</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_ttl">Roy Lichtenstein: Like New (Exhibit)</category>
      <media:content height="1799" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/10/08/multimedia/08cul-LICHTENSTEIN-whitney-02-hvkl/08cul-LICHTENSTEIN-whitney-02-hvkl-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800"></media:content>
      <media:credit>Marissa Alper for The New York Times</media:credit>
      <media:description>“New York World’s Fair Mural (Girl in Window)” by Roy Lichtenstein, from 1963, has been recreated and hand painted by Alex Da Corte’s studio. At 32 feet tall, on the Whitney’s terrace, it can be seen from the High Line.</media:description>
